{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters","id":1104181,"title":"[2E Fan] Imperial Practices \u2013 Magic of Archmasters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-15T23:49:26-07:00","id":1104181,"title":"[2E Fan] Imperial Practices \u2013 Magic of Archmasters","content":"As we are probably years till proper Archmasters rules beyond those pointed in 2E Mage corebook. Still, some of us want too use Invisible Masters as NPCs, so some rough ideas for spells of dots past 5 are sought out. So here is topic for our homebrews spells of archmages. For ease of reference and comparing, let\u2019s use main 2E spell format. This post will be edited with new spell proposed.<br /> For ease of reading, quick sum up of Imperial Practices from <b>Imperial Mysteries </b>book:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022: <i>The Practice of Dynamics</i></b><br /> This Practice allows archmages to create phenomena that change according to conditions \u2014 chain reactions that follow basic principles in a fractal manner without the caster\u2019s conscious direction or complex \u201cprogrammed\u201d effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022: <i>The Practice of Entities</i></b><br /> This Practice allows archmages to grant supernatural abilities to a target, incorporating the nature of an Arcanum into the target\u2019s pattern.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022: <i>The Practice of Excision</i></b><br /> Excision spells are clinical and often devastating removals of a pattern\u2019s proper-ties. Any interaction between a target and the Arcanum, a power, or part of a Template under the Arcanum\u2019s purview can be cut away.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022: <i>The Practice of Dominions</i></b><br /> The archmasters of the eighth degree learn how to make new worlds of their own. By re\ufb02ecting the Arcanum into the Golden Road, an archmaster can create Chantries, create self-sustaining ecosystems of spells to \ufb01 ll them, spawn Ochemata and other autonomous sub-souls to manage them, send those sub-souls into the Fallen World as her agents, and even create self-willed Artifacts by installing their own Gnosis into the creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: <i>The Practice of Transfiguration</i></b><br /> The most advanced and dedicated archmasters gain access to the ninth degree and the Practice of Trans\ufb01guration, which only contains one spell. By reversing the relationship between her enlightened soul and the Arcanum that is now so well-incorporated into it, the archmaster becomes the Arcanum, or more accurately, the Arcanum becomes the archmaster.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i><b>Prime</b></i><br /> <b>Arcanum Resistance</b> (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) by wyrdhamster<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Dynamics<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Occult, Science<br /> The mage can change Patter of Arcanum over target, making him resistant to any manipulation of this Arcanum. For each point of Potency on spell, target is resistant for one Arcanum in all alterations after the first in turn. Spell makes target resistant to first Arcanum-like power used on the target in particular turn. Till the time of next turn, any supernatural influence working under Arcanum principle are not working on the target \u2013 spells of particular Arcanum especially.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Time</b></i><br /> <b>Many Seconds in One</b> (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) by wyrdhamster<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Dynamics<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Intimidation, Science<br /> The mage can replicating flow of Time, allowing target to do many action in the same time. For each point of Potency on spell, target can do one more instant action per turn.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By cost of one Mana target can do number of spellcasting actions per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T23:54:25-07:00","id":1104184,"title":"","content":"Idea for <i>Arcanum Resistance</i> comes from my partner that advised me to look over AEGIS system from old <b>Secret World</b>, to make boss fights more interesting. Here is basic idea of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gZkYqKO1XeI\" data-code=\"gZkYqKO1XeI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gZkYqKO1XeI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T01:02:31-07:00","id":1104191,"title":"","content":"So it's a worse version of Wards and Signs. <br /> <br /> Reach on the Time spell should be +2, also I don't think I'd allow even archmasters to break the action economy of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T01:26:57-07:00","id":1104197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1104191#post1104191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's a worse version of Wards and Signs.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>Wards and Signs</i> still needs Potency to counter spells - <i>Arcanum Resistant</i> just kills spells cast on you. Finito. No Clash of Wills, no Potency comparison. Arcanum simply do not work on character.<br /> <br /> But I'm thinking about Reach option for <i>Arcanum Resistant </i>that let change Arcanum target is immune on Exceptional Success on other Arcanum target is attacked for. Like - first <i>Arcanum Resistant</i> is cast on character - then his enemies cast on him Matter spell. But his enemy then cast Spirit spell on Exp. Success - and Arcanum Resistant change on target to make him immune to Spirit now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1104191#post1104191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reach on the Time spell should be +2, also I don't think I'd allow even archmasters to break the action economy of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reach number is individual number. For example, other Time and Fate spells have their benefits stretche to spellcasting on +1 Reach, most of the examples in corebook.<br /> <br /> And they are all homebrewe spells - you are right to not let them be possible in you games. They are more ideas than basis of Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-16-2017, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T02:22:36-07:00","id":1104203,"title":"","content":"No, they're +2 Reach, check again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T03:21:48-07:00","id":1104210,"title":"","content":"I like these a lot.<br /> <br /> I would allow a Clash of Wills on Arcanum Resistant. Archmasters always win CoW against lesser beings by RAW now, so it won't break anything for your Cabal of Masters, but it will allow other Archmasters a chance to break through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T04:48:43-07:00","id":1104226,"title":"","content":"It's a smaller thing, but Imperial spells cannot be made into rotes.<br /> Each is so entirely unique there's no way to codify them into a formula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T04:55:39-07:00","id":1104229,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Arcanum Resistance be Excision practice? Also would have some heavy side effects, such as the target not being able to acess the arcanum anymore at the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T05:34:54-07:00","id":1104241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1104229#post1104229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Arcanum Resistance be Excision practice? Also would have some heavy side effects, such as the target not being able to acess the arcanum anymore at the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not severing the subject from the Arcanum. It's deploying a constantly shifting effect that defends against an Arcanum, which fits pretty thoroughly in Dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T08:47:12-07:00","id":1104310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1104241#post1104241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not severing the subject from the Arcanum. It's deploying a constantly shifting effect that defends against an Arcanum, which fits pretty thoroughly in Dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it shifting? It doesn't mention anything about anything shifting. I mean honestly it sounds mostly like shielding, but I could see an archmaster excising the ability of magic to affect a target with prime. Dynamics would be... a normal shielding spell that decides on its own which spells to hinder and which spells to allow based on your best interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T09:08:02-07:00","id":1104314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1104310#post1104310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it shifting? It doesn't mention anything about anything shifting. I mean honestly it sounds mostly like shielding, but I could see an archmaster excising the ability of magic to affect a target with prime. Dynamics would be... a normal shielding spell that decides on its own which spells to hinder and which spells to allow based on your best interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is constantly shifting to perfectly counter the magic directed at it, rendering such magic useless. It adapts to the magic cast at the archmaster, hence adjusting to the first thing fired at it:<br /> 'Spell makes target resistant to first Arcanum-like power used on the target in particular turn. Till the time of next turn, any supernatural influence working under Arcanum principle are not working on the target'<br /> <br /> It's the same way you can use Dynamics to perfectly bypass mage armor or any other kind of defense - it automatically probes weak spots and takes effect at full power. This is the same effect in reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T21:54:04-07:00","id":1105595,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it's actually a version of <i>Universal </i><i>Counterspell</i>, to me, which would normally Clash one specific effect. Making it work on multiple as needed sounds a fine example of Dynamics. Arguably, it wouldn't need Raises to target different arcana, either. It's not a bad idea; I would just prefer to simplify it.<br /> <br /> Since U.C. is an attainment, you could easily argue this is the 6 dot Prime Attainment on self and only need a spell to place it on someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 06-20-2017, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T22:57:03-07:00","id":1105608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1104210#post1104210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow a Clash of Wills on Arcanum Resistant. Archmasters always win CoW against lesser beings by RAW now, so it won't break anything for your Cabal of Masters, but it will allow other Archmasters a chance to break through.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Archmastery Practices CAN be used on lesser beings as targets. In <b>Imperial Mysteries </b>there is whole story seed ideas that normal mages cabal is contracted by Archmaster for his quests with a promise on Archmage using his one of powers for the wonder normal PCs need for.<br /> <br /> And if cast <i>Arcanum Resistance</i> on those non-Archmasters, Clash of Wills would make this spell nothing different than <i>Wards and Signs </i>( as you would compare Potency )<i>.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T22:57:03-07:00","id":1105609,"title":"","content":"( Sorry, double post. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T01:22:24-07:00","id":1105632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104181-2e-fan-imperial-practices-\u2013-magic-of-archmasters?p=1105608#post1105608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if cast <i>Arcanum Resistance</i> on those non-Archmasters, Clash of Wills would make this spell nothing different than <i>Wards and Signs </i>( as you would compare Potency )<i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No it wouldn't. Anything targeting them would Clash against the Archmaster, not the person he put it on. The creator is the one that Clashes, not the subject.<br /> <br /> Since lesser beings can never win a CoW against Archmasters, that would mean that any normal mages he put the spell on would gain the effects as intended *unless* they're fighting another Archmaster, who would be able to Clash vs the first one to effect them normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}